node_modules/
.wrangler/
.dev.vars

# Historical-import and audit runtime state: resume cursors, progress logs, supervisor output, the
# JSON/text artifacts each measurement script writes beside itself.
# Machine-local and rewritten constantly; committing them would create noise and could resurrect a
# stale cursor on another checkout, making a resumed import skip records it never actually created.
#
# Broadened from the three explicit patterns it started as: every one of these scripts writes its
# output to a dotfile next to itself, so naming them one at a time only ever caught up after the fact
# (.relations.out, .audit-*.json, .supervisor-contacts.out and a dozen others were all missed). No
# dotfile under scripts/ is tracked, so the wildcard loses nothing.
scripts/.*
